Herald is mundane and godly at the same time. They are the most average of all, an amalgam of everyone you’ve ever seen, and yet they exude a dignity that almost compels one to worship them. If, however, one pierces past the glamer the Herald insists upon, they will see the strange anatomy lying beneath. A chin, cleft completely in twain, forms jagged mandibles. Small dotted secondary eyes orbit the two humanoid ones. Antennae sprout from the forehead. A circular horn-like protrusion sprouts from the chest.

A likeness of Herald, a horned humanoid atop a mountain of corpses, stands on one of the six god doors in the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]]. Behind the door is an armory.

The saboteur in [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei/index|Iomenei]], the elven fluid master [[People/Gerhard|Gerhard]], has a jaw split into mandibles and small closed eyelids dotted around his eyes, and scratched the mark of a horn inside a circle into the bedpost where he slept. His sabotage is driven by religious devotion.

The Machine God, an old [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] in the lower hull of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], says Herald wormed its way into the strider's first inhabitants over years and centuries until they were taken and changed. What is left of them still crawls about the strider, and followers of Herald remain there, spread through the interior and keeping little contact with one another.

The followers who came to the strider with him are called the true kin there. They sleep in a onetime hospital on the strider's third floor, waiting on the end of the journey, while a few keepers walk the halls and tend them.
